# Connected vehicles / telematics — MASSIVE FAN-IN, tiny fan-out.
#
# Millions of vehicles publishing telemetry to their own topic; a handful of
# backend consumers read through ONE $share group. Huge connection count,
# LOW per-client rate, QoS 1 (trip data loss matters).
#
# The per-client rate is deliberately 1 msg/s. emqtt-bench's QoS 1 publish is
# SYNCHRONOUS (one PUBACK round trip per client at a time), so a high per-client
# rate makes the LOAD GENERATOR the limit, not the broker — measured 2026-08-26:
# at 10 msg/s x 100K clients the brokers sat at 39-44% CPU while 97% of
# publishes ran late. At 1 msg/s the ack round trip has room and the number is
# the BROKER's.
LANES=B
LANE_B_QOS=1
LANE_B_FANOUT=0
LANE_B_PUBS_OVERRIDE=100000
LANE_B_SUBS_OVERRIDE=100
LANE_B_PUB_CONTAINERS=5
LANE_B_SUB_CONTAINERS=1
LANE_B_RUNGS_OVERRIDE="100000"
# Sweep the workload's own axis by overriding the population per run:
#   LANE_B_PUBS_OVERRIDE=25000|50000|100000|200000 (with the rung = pubs x 1/s)
# Tuning levers: MQTTD_RECEIVE_MAXIMUM, MQTTD_MAX_CONNECTIONS,
#   MQTTD_DURABLE_SESSIONS on/off, MQTTD_MAX_INFLIGHT_MESSAGES.

# ── why this workload overrides two more knobs (2026-08-26 run, corrected) ───
# The first run of this shape produced a curve-shaped set of numbers that was
# not a measurement of the broker. Both ends of the harness were the limit and
# the brokers idled near 50% CPU throughout. Two independent causes:
#
#  * N=1 — the rig template caps at MQTTD_MAX_CONNECTIONS=60000 (sized for lane
#    C's 50k lane). This shape asks for 100 100. The broker rejected 8620 at
#    admission and the reconnect churn produced 79 524 tcp_closed publish
#    errors. At one node the workload could not run at all.
#  * N=3/N=5 — all 100 100 connected, zero rejections, yet the brokers dropped
#    72 597 messages at N=3 with reason="pending-cap". 100 000 publishers fed a
#    $share group of just 100 subscribers, and this rig's own measured ceiling
#    is ~1000 msg/s per subscriber — so 100 subs IS the offered rate with no
#    headroom. The subscribers were the wall; the broker dropped the rest.
#
# 420 subscribers gives 4.2x headroom so the BROKER is the constraint. The cap is
# lifted for THIS workload only, through the rig's per-variant hook, so no other
# shape's disclosed conditions change and the override lands in the archived env
# dumps — a variant can never run undisclosed.
LANE_B_SUBS_OVERRIDE=420
EXTRA_BROKER_ENV="MQTTD_MAX_CONNECTIONS=150000
MQTTD_MAX_SESSIONS=150000"
